From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:54:40 +0900
Subject: kscreenosd: read the KScreen configuration at startup

KScreenOSDUtil never called retrieveKScreen(), so its output count stayed 0 and plugging a display
never switched to convergence (docked) mode.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain bug; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:cast.agent_screen
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/58
---
 quicksettings/kscreenosd/kscreenosdutil.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/quicksettings/kscreenosd/kscreenosdutil.cpp b/quicksettings/kscreenosd/kscreenosdutil.cpp
index d5db928..bce4069 100644
--- a/quicksettings/kscreenosd/kscreenosdutil.cpp
+++ b/quicksettings/kscreenosd/kscreenosdutil.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@ KScreenOSDUtil::KScreenOSDUtil(QObject *parent)
         }
         setOutputs(m_config->outputs().size());
     });
+    // Without a config the output count stays 0 and KScreenOSDProvider never
+    // switches to docked (convergence) mode when a display is added (docs/58).
+    retrieveKScreen();
 }
 
 void KScreenOSDUtil::retrieveKScreen()
